          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"category\":\"intermittent_DAQ_or_digitizer_readout_dropout\",\"cause\":\"unknown\",\"action\":\"First compare channel-presence timelines with digitizer-board boundaries and the anomaly onset by subrun. Check MilliDAQ/DAQ logs for restarts, readout errors, synchronization loss, queue saturation, or high CPU usage, and compare digitizer event rates against trigger-board rates. If omissions align with one digitizer, inspect its synchronization and lock state and conditionally restart that digitizer/DAQ PC using the approved procedure; if omissions are system-wide and coincide with a DAQ restart or CPU saturation, conditionally restart MilliDAQ or address the host load instead. Do not pursue PMT/HV repairs unless HV logs or channel-local pulse/LVDS behavior independently supports them.\",\"confidence\":0.58,\"supporting_historical_runs\":[1500,1604,1605,1620],\"reasoning_summary\":\"OBSERVED: anomalies affect 65/86 subruns with 936 entries, including many missing-channel flags and extreme nPulses_median outliers across multiple channels. Trigger rate is stable near 2.37, and all 48 LVDS signal pins have persistent nonzero, broadly similar counts with no strong pin transition. The count drop near subrun 40 occurs without a comparable rate anomaly and may reflect exposure length rather than detector behavior. INFERRED: healthy trigger/LVDS summaries argue against a trigger-board or localized LVDS failure and make an intermittent downstream DAQ/digitizer readout problem more plausible. Runs 1500, 1604, 1605, and 1620 provide partial analogies involving pulse-count anomalies with DAQ restart, high CPU, or digitizer lockup, but there is no exact historical match. A PMT-base failure is less supported because the pattern is widespread and no abnormal LVDS pin is reported. UNKNOWN: digitizer rates, board grouping of missing channels, synchronization/lock status, CPU and queue telemetry, restart logs, within-run configuration changes, and HV status are required to distinguish DAQ restart, host overload, digitizer lockup, or data-processing artifacts.\"}"
        }
      ],
